# Improved AMP (0.1.0-experimental): the AMP envelope is heard. BD hits by MIDI note, on the BD's own
# output, the AMP page set by CC: ATK 0, HLD 0, DEC 55 (25ms on the page) is a short hit; DEC 89 (300ms)
# rings longer; ATK 45 (15.0ms) reaches its top later and as high (the decay waits for the attack);
# DEC 127 (INF) rings for as long as the BD's own sound does.
# The BD's other settings are the kit's, so the checks compare hits with each other: the track needs a
# sound that rings for 3 s or more with the AMP envelope open (a sample, or a long synth decay).
# Measured on the unit, from RAM, 10 Nov 2026 (five runs): len20 short 9.5 to 10.0, long 102.5,
# slow 24.5 to 25.0, inf 2941.0 to 2942.5 (one run 2858.0; the window ends at 3000); attack short 1.0, slow 15.5; peak -12.4 to -12.3 dBFS in all four.
# Changes the BD track's AMP page in the active kit and does not put it back. It ends on the short decay,
# so the track is silent when the case is over.
# For the unit: rytm-emu's analog voice follows these settings only roughly (measured: len20 1,
# 7 and 22 ms where the unit has 10, 103 and 135), so its sound is no reference.
name: improved-amp-sound
state: changes
target: unit

hold TRK
key BD
release TRK
key AMP
cc 78 0
cc 79 0
cc 80 55
cc 81 0
cc 82 0
cc 83 0
cc 10 64
cc 7 100
wait 300
audio short BD 1200
wait 50
note BD
wait 1300
cc 80 89
wait 300
audio long BD 1200
wait 50
note BD
wait 1300
cc 80 55
cc 78 45
wait 300
audio slow BD 1200
wait 50
note BD
wait 1300
cc 78 0
cc 80 127
wait 300
audio inf BD 3000
wait 50
note BD
wait 3100
cc 80 55
wait 300
note BD
wait 500
audio rest BD 300
wait 400

expect short.hits == 1
expect long.hits == 1
expect slow.hits == 1
expect short.onset == 55 within 10
expect long.len20 > short.len20 + 50
expect slow.attack == short.attack + 14.5 within 3
expect slow.peak == short.peak within 1
expect inf.len20 > 2900
expect rest.peak < short.peak - 40
